WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.000
Movie there is no spoon

00:02.520 --> 00:05.400
Albert Einstein once said reality is merely an illusion

00:05.960 --> 00:07.960
albeit a very persistent one a

00:08.360 --> 00:14.660
Fascinating thought isn't it we stand at the crossroads of science and perception questioning the very fabric of our existence

00:14.760 --> 00:20.160
We explore the concept of reality as understood in the realms of physics and philosophy

00:20.800 --> 00:24.560
Preparing ourselves for a deeper plunge into this profound subject

00:25.040 --> 00:29.360
But what if what we perceive as reality is not as it seems?

00:30.000 --> 00:35.920
What if there is no spoon welcome to the world of quantum mechanics where nothing is as it appears?

00:36.840 --> 00:41.120
Here we delve into a realm that defies our everyday understanding of reality

00:41.880 --> 00:44.820
Picture if you will a particle that also behaves like a wave

00:45.200 --> 00:50.440
This is the essence of wave particle duality a cornerstone of quantum mechanics

00:50.680 --> 00:55.480
It's as if you could be in two places at once a seemingly impossible feat

00:56.040 --> 00:58.040
Now consider Heisenberg's

00:58.200 --> 01:05.080
Uncertainty principle it tells us that the more we know about a particle's position the less we know about its speed and vice versa

01:05.480 --> 01:10.840
It's like trying to catch a slippery fish with bare hands the more you try to grip it the faster

01:10.840 --> 01:15.520
It slips away these oddities of the quantum world baffle even the brightest minds

01:15.960 --> 01:22.880
They challenge our conventional understanding of reality leading us to question what we perceive as real in the quantum world

01:22.880 --> 01:24.960
It seems that there really is no spoon

01:25.480 --> 01:30.440
But it's not just the quantum world that challenges our perception of reality our very own brains do too

01:31.240 --> 01:37.400
Indeed our brains are the artists of our reality painting a picture based on the sensory information they receive

01:38.040 --> 01:43.640
However, this interpretation isn't always accurate. Just think about optical illusions

01:44.280 --> 01:52.760
Where what we see contradicts physical reality or consider auditory misperceptions where we hear sounds that aren't truly present

01:53.280 --> 01:58.400
So in a sense our brains are constantly creating and recreating the spoon

01:58.680 --> 02:02.760
So are we living in a matrix like world where reality is not what it seems?

02:03.560 --> 02:10.640
We've delved into the peculiarities of quantum mechanics the fascinating role our brain plays in crafting our perception and the profound

02:10.960 --> 02:18.140
Philosophical notions these insights stir we've wrestled with the question of reality and it seems much like the matrix

02:18.140 --> 02:20.440
It may not be as straightforward as we once believed

02:21.080 --> 02:24.680
Perhaps there is no spoon perhaps reality is not what it seems

02:24.840 --> 02:29.520
But in the end it is our persistent illusion and we must navigate it as best we can

